<h1>Hardware Settings - Sensor Tab</h1>
<hr align="left" width="100.526%" size="5" class="whs3">
<p class="description"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description: Sensor</b></span> Tab changes options related to the sensor settings.</p>
<p><img src="../Images/sensor_tab.bmp" width="551px" height="488px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">The tab is divided in four sections and a checkbox for 'Certified settings':</span></p>
<p class="sub-head">Profiles <a href="Profiles_in_HW_settings_(MMX,_MMZ,_MMC).htm"><img src="../../../../Corrosion/Images/i_blue_sm.jpg" width="23px" height="16px" border="0" class="img_whs5" alt=""></a></p>
<p class="parameterdescription">&#160;</p>
<p class="sub-head"><span style="text-decoration:none;">L</span>aser Power section</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Click and drag the <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>'Laser Power'</b></span> indicator to the desired setting or type-in the percentage in the box right to the slider. (0 is the minimum, 100 the maximum) The default value is 25%.</p>
<p id="p1" class="Note"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Note</b></span>: For MM C sensors 'Laser power' slider means percentage of the allowed range of the laser power. For example, if laser power is restricted to level 2 then value of 25 means 25% of 2, which is level 0.5.</p>
<p id="p1">&#160;</p>
<p class="sub-head"><span style="text-decoration:none;">Ambient Threshold section</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle">Value edit box</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">This box contains the ambient threshold setting of the current material item option. Sets the sensitivity of the sensor to surrounding light. A high value is used in a bright environment, a lower value in a darker environment. Lower values can be better at picking up darker colours. Default value is 96.</p>
<p class="parameterstitle">Threshold filling</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">If enabled this option allows achieving better results when scanning dark surfaces and very shiny surfaces with reflections. The appropriate laser power and threshold values must be used in these cases. The option is available for MMD and MMC sensors only.</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">&#160;</p>
<p class="sub-head">Info section</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Displays versions of the built-in software for controlling the sensor.</p>
<p>&#160;</p>
<p class="sub-head">Sensor section</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Sensor type, Sensor serial number, Date of manufacture, and Temperature (internal temperature of the sensor) will be automatically detected by the software for D sensors.</p>
<p>&#160;</p>
<p class="sub-head">Sensor detection section</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">If <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Auto</b></span> is selected then KUBE tries detecting all types of sensors until it finds the installed one. If set to <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Manual</b></span> then KUBE tries to detect only the sensor type, which is selected in the listbox. In case of fault it doesn't detect other types. Currently available options are 'MM X/Y', 'MM Z', 'MM D/C', and 'None'.</p>
<p>&#160;</p>
<p class="sub-head">Refresh MMIB/Sensor status button</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">This button is used to refresh the settings if a sensor is changed. This includes MMIB/sensor detection and loading the corresponding calibration file for the detected sensor.</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">&#160;</p>
<p class="sub-head">Advanced Settings dialog</p>
<p class="whs6"><img src="../../MMX/X_Hardware_Sensor_Advanced_Settings.gif" width="531px" height="195px" border="0" class="img_whs7" alt=""></p>
<p class="parameterstitle">Field of view</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Adjusts the stripe width of the sensor, giving more control over the data captured.</p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet">Wide' uses full stripe width. Enabled by default.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet">Normal' restricts the stripe width (varies for different sensors).</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>'</b></span>Limit effective stripe' checkbox to manually select the stripe width. Default value for stripe width is 20mm. Default value for Limit effective width is off.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p>&#160;</p>
<p class="sub-head">Certified Settings checkbox</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">When this option is enabled all settings in the tab are set to their default values. For the best results, it is recommended to use 'Certified settings'.</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">When all changes are made, confirm with <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>'</b></span><span class="Button" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Apply'</b></span> button.</p>
